---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout current="harness-engineering" title="Harness engineering">
  <section class="section page-section">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Runtime discipline</p>
      <h1>Harness engineering: where agents become software.</h1>
      <p>
        Tracing is the post-mortem. The harness is the runtime boundary that
        enforces the same safety and logic rails on the next run.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mini-diagram react-diagram harness-diagram" aria-label="Agent harness responsibility map" style="margin-bottom: 48px; margin-left: -40px; margin-right: -40px; border-radius: 20px;">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 1080 440" role="img">
        <defs>
          <marker id="harness-arrow" markerHeight="8" markerWidth="8" orient="auto" refX="7" refY="4">
            <path d="M0,0 L8,4 L0,8 Z" fill="var(--accent)"></path>
          </marker>
        </defs>

        <!-- Big Harness Container -->
        <rect x="300" y="20" width="480" height="400" rx="24" fill="var(--surface-muted)" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="8 4"></rect>
        <text x="540" y="60" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted)" font-size="16" font-weight="700" letter-spacing="0.08em" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, monospace">HARNESS BOUNDARY</text>

        <!-- Connection Lines -->
        <g class="harness-links" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-dasharray="8 8" style="animation: data-flow 1.5s linear infinite; opacity: 0.8;">
          <!-- Inputs to boundary -->
          <path d="M 220 114 H 298" marker-end="url(#harness-arrow)"></path>
          <path d="M 220 220 H 298" marker-end="url(#harness-arrow)"></path>
          <path d="M 220 326 H 298" marker-end="url(#harness-arrow)"></path>

          <!-- Boundary to Outputs -->
          <path d="M 780 114 H 858" marker-end="url(#harness-arrow)"></path>
          <path d="M 780 220 H 858" marker-end="url(#harness-arrow)"></path>
          <path d="M 780 326 H 858" marker-end="url(#harness-arrow)"></path>

          <!-- Internal Flow -->
          <path d="M 520 114 H 568" marker-end="url(#harness-arrow)"></path>
          <path d="M 680 144 V 190" marker-end="url(#harness-arrow)"></path>
          <path d="M 680 250 V 296" marker-end="url(#harness-arrow)"></path>
          <path d="M 580 326 H 522" marker-end="url(#harness-arrow)"></path>
          <path d="M 420 296 V 144" marker-end="url(#harness-arrow)"></path>
        </g>

        <!-- Node styles overrides to make them larger than default -->
        <style>
          .harness-diagram text { font-size: 18px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
        </style>

        <!-- Input Nodes -->
        <g class="react-node-svg">
          <rect x="20" y="84" width="200" height="60" rx="12"></rect>
          <text x="120" y="114">User goal</text>
        </g>
        <g class="react-node-svg">
          <rect x="20" y="190" width="200" height="60" rx="12"></rect>
          <text x="120" y="220">Session state</text>
        </g>
        <g class="react-node-svg">
          <rect x="20" y="296" width="200" height="60" rx="12"></rect>
          <text x="120" y="326">Available tools</text>
        </g>

        <!-- Internal Nodes -->
        <g class="react-node-svg is-planner">
          <rect x="320" y="84" width="200" height="60" rx="30"></rect>
          <text x="420" y="114">Build context</text>
        </g>
        <g class="react-node-svg">
          <rect x="580" y="84" width="200" height="60" rx="30"></rect>
          <text x="680" y="114">Route tools</text>
        </g>
        <g class="react-node-svg is-critic">
          <rect x="580" y="190" width="200" height="60" rx="30"></rect>
          <text x="680" y="220">Gate actions</text>
        </g>
        <g class="react-node-svg">
          <rect x="580" y="296" width="200" height="60" rx="30"></rect>
          <text x="680" y="326">Commit events</text>
        </g>
        <g class="react-node-svg is-done">
          <rect x="320" y="296" width="200" height="60" rx="30"></rect>
          <text x="420" y="326">Stop / continue</text>
        </g>

        <!-- Output Nodes -->
        <g class="react-node-svg">
          <rect x="860" y="84" width="200" height="60" rx="12"></rect>
          <text x="960" y="114">Observations</text>
        </g>
        <g class="react-node-svg">
          <rect x="860" y="190" width="200" height="60" rx="12"></rect>
          <text x="960" y="220">Artifacts</text>
        </g>
        <g class="react-node-svg">
          <rect x="860" y="296" width="200" height="60" rx="12"></rect>
          <text x="960" y="326">Trace + eval data</text>
        </g>
      </svg>
    </div>

    <p class="map-caption">
      Inputs flow in. The harness shapes every turn. Evidence flows out.
    </p>

    <div class="section-head compact-head" style="margin-top: 56px;">
      <p class="eyebrow">The loop</p>
      <h2>Three slots, every turn.</h2>
    </div>

    <ul class="timeline-list">
      <li>
        <span class="timeline-number">01</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Before the model</strong>
          <p>Load the context, assemble the instructions, and expose the available tools.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="timeline-number">02</span>
        <div>
          <strong>During tool execution</strong>
          <p>Enforce security policies, gate sensitive actions, and capture the tool observations.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="timeline-number">03</span>
        <div>
          <strong>After the turn</strong>
          <p>Commit state deltas, update the persistent session history, and append the trace data.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="section-head compact-head" style="margin-top: 56px;">
      <p class="eyebrow">Where the effort moved</p>
      <h2>From <em>prompt</em> engineering to <em>context</em> engineering to <em>harness</em> engineering.</h2>
      <p>
        Each step adds a layer of control without removing the layers
        underneath. Prompts still matter; context still matters. The
        change is where the <em>load-bearing</em> work happens now — and
        which failures the team treats as engineering bugs rather than
        prompt-tuning chores.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ol class="shift-track">
      <li class="shift-stage" data-step="1">
        <span class="shift-stage__kicker">Stage 01</span>
        <h3>Prompt engineering</h3>
        <p class="shift-stage__lede">Tune the words you send.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>One model call.</strong> One carefully written prompt.</li>
          <li><strong>Wording problems.</strong> Failures look like wording problems; fixes are edits.</li>
          <li><strong>Fragile scaling.</strong> Caps out fast as soon as state, tools, or branches enter.</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li class="shift-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="shift-arrow__badge">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" role="presentation">
            <path d="M5 12h14m-6-6 6 6-6 6"></path>
          </svg>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="shift-stage" data-step="2">
        <span class="shift-stage__kicker">Stage 02</span>
        <h3>Context engineering</h3>
        <p class="shift-stage__lede">Build the right inputs.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Dynamic assembly.</strong> Retrieval, memory, tool selection, schemas, examples.</li>
          <li><strong>Just-in-time state.</strong> Each turn assembles the context the model actually needs.</li>
          <li><strong>Visibility bugs.</strong> Failures move from wording to <em>what the model can see</em>.</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li class="shift-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="shift-arrow__badge">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" role="presentation">
            <path d="M5 12h14m-6-6 6 6-6 6"></path>
          </svg>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="shift-stage is-now" data-step="3">
        <span class="shift-stage__kicker">Stage 03 · here</span>
        <h3>Harness engineering</h3>
        <p class="shift-stage__lede">Make the runtime enforce it.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Control boundaries.</strong> Approval gates, eval files, event logs, HITL pauses, trajectory checks.</li>
          <li><strong>Invariants in code.</strong> Logic lives around the loop, not in the prompt.</li>
          <li><strong>Testable regressions.</strong> Failures become structural regressions the team can test for.</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
    </ol>


  </section>
</SiteLayout>
